   "text": "I used UUIDv4 for every primary key on a payments service because \"distributed systems need it.\" Two years later the buffer pool was 80 percent index pages. The table had 120 million rows. The primary key index alone was 18 GB. A BIGINT version of the same workload sat at 4.2 GB."
