   ],
   "hook_chars": 45,
   "text": "THINGS THAT QUIETLY KILL ENGINEERING CAREERS:"
  },
  {
   "rank": 40,
   "id": "17933389851406827",
   "views": 293,
   "likes": 0,
   "replies": 4,
   "date": "2026-10-16",
   "permalink": "https://www.threads.com/@owlsky17/post/DekWUNbGZNq",
   "format": "sentence_statement",
   "topic": "sql_postgres_orm",
   "topics": [
    "sql_postgres_orm"
   ],
   "hook_chars": 235,
   "text": "---\nThe dumbest performance bug I've seen in production wasn't a missing index. It was a UUIDv4 primary key on a high-write table being used as the clustering key, which turned every insert into random I/O across 12 shards of Postgres."
  },
  {
   "rank": 41,
   "id": "18103808978194846",
   "views": 293,
   "likes": 2,
   "replies": 6,
   "date": "2026-10-10",
   "permalink": "https://www.threads.com/@owlsky17/post/DeTttiUm4Gf",
   "format": "sentence_story",
   "topic": "career_senior",
   "topics": [
    "career_senior"
   ],
   "hook_chars": 95,
   "text": "I used to think senior engineers wrote better code. Then I saw what they actually optimize for."
  },
  {
   "rank": 42,
   "id": "18125872771859046",
   "views": 285,
   "likes": 0,
   "replies": 6,
   "date": "2026-10-18",
   "permalink": "https://www.threads.com/@owlsky17/post/DeoQnJaFveo",
   "format": "sentence_statement",
   "topic": "sql_postgres_orm",
   "topics": [
    "sql_postgres_orm"
   ],
   "hook_chars": 281,
   "text": "An ORM transaction held a row lock for 47 seconds while waiting on an external HTTP call. The lock chain: UPDATE users SET last_login=now() WHERE id=123 -> SELECT FOR UPDATE on orders -> HTTP POST to payment gateway -> COMMIT. Every concurrent login for that user queued behind it."
  },
  {
   "rank": 43,
   "id": "18343392172285452",
   "views": 282,
   "likes": 0,
   "replies": 5,
   "date": "2026-10-15",
   "permalink": "https://www.threads.com/@owlsky17/post/DegfIwXFsox",
   "format": "sentence_statement",
   "topic": "sql_postgres_orm",
   "topics": [
    "sql_postgres_orm"
   ],
   "hook_chars": 190,
   "text": "Stop using UUIDs as primary keys. They destroy write performance, bloat indexes by 4x, and you almost certainly don't need them. Your database is paying a tax for a scale you will never hit."
  },
  {
   "rank": 44,
   "id": "17940652383385518",
   "views": 268,
   "likes": 0,
   "replies": 5,
   "date": "2026-10-15",
   "permalink": "https://www.threads.com/@owlsky17/post/DehV37QIG8Q",
   "format": "sentence_statement",
   "topic": "career_senior",
   "topics": [
    "career_senior",
    "sql_postgres_orm"
   ],
   "hook_chars": 138,
   "text": "If API p99 is rising while Postgres CPU stays low, check pool wait time before adding database capacity. Most teams scale the wrong layer."
  },
  {
   "rank": 45,
   "id": "18498737971101391",
   "views": 261,
   "likes": 0,
   "replies": 4,
   "date": "2026-10-17",
   "permalink": "https://www.threads.com/@owlsky17/post/DelDUsAjd-o",
   "format": "sentence_statement",
   "topic": "sql_postgres_orm",
   "topics": [
    "sql_postgres_orm"
   ],
   "hook_chars": 129,
   "text": "production-cost reveal: a UUIDv4 index can hurt write performance, but here is how to measure whether it matters in your workload"
  },
